### What Are Common Interview Follow-Up Questions?

Interviewers commonly ask:

- Implement the Trie from scratch (TrieNode class, insert, search, startsWith).
- Why store the full word on the terminal node instead of a boolean flag? For O(1) collection without path reconstruction.
- How would you handle uppercase and special characters? Expand the children array or use a HashMap.
- What if the dictionary is dynamic (words added during search)? The Trie supports incremental insertion.

```java
package com.bank.core;

public class TrieOperations {
    static class TrieNode {
        TrieNode[] children = new TrieNode[26];
        boolean isEnd = false;
        String word = null;
    }

    public static boolean search(TrieNode root, String word) {
        TrieNode node = root;
        for (char c : word.toCharArray()) {
            if (node.children[c - 'a'] == null) return false;
            node = node.children[c - 'a'];
        }
        return node.isEnd;
    }
}
```
